ng that history-defining figures still share the human fate of ordinary death. The ninth lesson: the measure of a leader is not how he dies, but how his structures endure. Genghis Khan confronted mortality not as a defeat but as a final transition in a life defined by purpose.", "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2", "voice_settings": {"stability": 0.55, "similarity_boost": 0.85, "style": 0.15, "use_speaker_boost": true}}' \
