    -H "Accept: audio/mpeg" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -H "xi-api-key: ${API_KEY}" \
    -d '{"text": "Hannibal’s ability to adapt under extreme constraints may be his most underrated genius. He did not command a stable empire, nor did he operate from a secure homeland. He faced political hesitation from Carthage, unreliable allies, a hostile Italy, unpredictable seasons, and constant Roman pressure. Yet he transformed this unstable environment into a strategic advantage. Hannibal treated constraints as signals that revealed hidden opportunities. When lacking supplies, he repositioned to regions with local abundance. When outnumbered, he lured Rome into terrain that neutralized numerical superiority. When his cavalry outperformed Roman horsemen, he built strategies around mobility and envelopment. Adaptation for Hannibal was not reactive improvisation but deliberate structural flexibility. His army was designed to pivot across roles, terrains, and seasons. Strategy shifted fluidly based on the internal state of his forces and the external behavior of Rome. Modern strategy often glorifies ideal conditions, but Hannibal’s legacy shows that mastery arises from navigating imperfection. Constraints focus creativity. They sharpen perception, accelerate learning, and reveal the true nature of the adversary. Hannibal demonstrates that the greatest strategist is not the one who controls everything but the one who thrives when nothing is controllable. His model is essential today for leaders facing volatile markets, shifting geopolitical landscapes, and disruptive technologies.", "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2", "voice_settings": {"stability": 0.55, "similarity_boost": 0.85, "style": 0.15, "use_speaker_boost": true}}' \
