    -d '{"text": "Hannibal’s march over the Alps into Italy is one of history’s most dramatic acts of power projection. Yet the same distance that magnified the shock also deepened his strategic vulnerability. Operating far from home turned every success into a harder problem. First, his line of communication to Carthage was thin and intermittent. Reinforcements, money, and supplies had to cross seas contested by Rome, then land on shores where Roman fleets and armies could interfere. The farther he advanced into Italy, the longer and more fragile these lines became. Second, Hannibal lacked a secure base in Italy itself. He captured cities and made alliances, but he never obtained a coastal stronghold fully safe from Roman counterattack, nor a region so loyal that it could serve as a reliable industrial and logistical heart. He moved like a knife but never built a hand to wield it steadily. Third, distance meant information lag. Carthaginian leaders could not see the war as he saw it; he could not know their debates in real time. Strategic coordination across such gaps required a maturity that Carthage did not always show. Rome, by contrast, fought near its core, with shorter lines of communication between battlefield, Senate, and supply. Fourth, operating far from home shaped local perceptions. Italian communities understood that Hannibal might win battles, but Rome would still be there centuries later. Aligning with the distant Carthaginian general risked retribution once he left or lost. Without a visible, stable Carthaginian presence, many sat on the fence or offered lukewarm support. The lesson for modern strategists is that projecting power far from home multiplies both possibilities and perils. Distance stretches logistics, distorts information, complicates politics, and changes how locals calculate risk. Hannibal shows that spectacular entry is not enough; an expeditionary strategy must include building a second home in the theater—or accept that every kilometer gained is also another thread of vulnerability.", "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2", "voice_settings": {"stability": 0.55, "similarity_boost": 0.85, "style": 0.15, "use_speaker_boost": true}}' \
