    -H "xi-api-key: ${API_KEY}" \
    -d '{"text": "Tonight you are allowed to rest. You do not have to solve anything or fix your whole life in a single thought. Imagine your body as a quiet river finally reaching a wide gentle lake. The water is still moving but slowly and softly almost like breathing. With every breath out the river carries a little weight away from your shoulders and a little noise away from your mind. The day can loosen its hands now. Every message every unfinished task every complicated feeling can stay on the shore. They are still there but they no longer need you right now. What matters is this small island of time where you are allowed to be only one thing simply a human being who is tired and deserves care. You feel your spine resting against the bed the pillow under your head the blanket like a light protective cloud over your body. Your jaw softens your eyes grow heavy your hands lie open and harmless by your sides. You do not have to hold on so tightly anymore. The world can spin without your effort for a while. Somewhere far away your worries are slowly wrapped in soft cloth placed in a quiet box and carried to another room. You will meet them again when you are stronger and calmer. For now they become distant shapes fading into a gentle background that does not need your attention. You are not running away from responsibility you are refilling the lamp so it can shine tomorrow. Each breath in is a small kindness and each breath out is a small release. A thought may try to pull you back into planning or replaying but you can let it pass like a small boat gliding across the lake from one shore to the other without stopping. You remain the water itself deep and steady underneath. In this depth nothing urgent exists. There is only the slow rhythm of your heart the soft music of your lungs and the simple truth that you have done enough for today. Even if something felt unfinished you still carried yourself through another day of being alive and that is already a quiet kind of courage. Let that be enough for tonight. You can rest inside that truth like resting your head on a familiar warm chest feeling safety and softness around you. Little by little your mind settles like fine sand sinking to the bottom of clear water and the surface of your awareness becomes smooth and calm ready to welcome the gentle light of sleep.", "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2", "voice_settings": {"stability": 0.55, "similarity_boost": 0.85, "style": 0.15, "use_speaker_boost": true}}' \
