arm place in the hollow of a tree. Feel how the night wraps around you not as a threat but as a soft blanket that covers noise and sharp edges. Every breath deepens the shelter around you and every exhale invites your body to sink a little further into trust. You are not behind. You are not late. You are simply here in a friendly forest that is large enough to hold both your weariness and your hope. You can let night carry you now.", "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2", "voice_settings": {"stability": 0.55, "similarity_boost": 0.85, "style": 0.15, "use_speaker_boost": true}}' \
